Overview:

Frontier models have already absorbed most of the public internet and generalist tasks, but they still lack the tacit judgment of experts who do complex professional work for a living. Bridging this gap requires identifying, verifying, and engaging a significant number of experts across many, often niche, domains over an extended period of time. And the specificity matters: not a physician, but an investigator who has actually run a Phase III oncology trial; not a generalist consultant, but a reimbursement lead who has negotiated with payers. &nbsp;

Guidepoint Labs' human data team is leading the way to solve exactly that problem for frontier model builders and researchers &nbsp;building frontier models, having access on day one to millions of vetted experts across effectively every industry and deep into the sub-specialties, along with mature governance, compliance, and confidentiality infrastructure. &nbsp;

As a Strategic Project Lead, you own a lab's project from the first scoping call to the last accepted batch. You turn a researcher's goal into a spec, build the expert team that can deliver it, hold the quality bar, and run the numbers so the work pays for itself. &nbsp;

This is an operator role. You will spend your days in specs, spreadsheets, expert channels and calls with researchers. You will work with lab researchers and research PMs on one side, and with Guidepoint's network, recruiting, compliance and engineering teams on the other. &nbsp;

As a team building something new, we offer a growth path that’s shaped by your contributions rather than tenure. People who excel in managing their projects can grow into larger accounts, team leadership, and their own book of business. &nbsp;

This role is hybrid working out of our New York City Headquarters.&nbsp;

What Y ou'll Do:

• Run delivery end to end. &nbsp;Scope with the lab, write the spec, set the timeline and staffing plan, and drive each project through pilot, calibration, ramp and acceptance. Expect 2 to 4 projects at once. &nbsp;

• Be the lab's operator. &nbsp;Serve as a point of contact for researchers and research PMs. Report on a set cadence, flag risk before it lands, and turn good delivery into the next scope. &nbsp;

• Build expert teams fast. &nbsp;Work with Guidepoint's network and recruiting teams to find, vet, onboard and manage experts (physicians, lawyers, analysts, engineers, PhDs), from 20 people to several hundred per project. &nbsp;

• Deliver quality. &nbsp;Write guidelines and rubrics, run calibration rounds, audit output, and fix root causes before the lab ever sees the problem. &nbsp;

• Own the economics. &nbsp;Track throughput, cost per task, expert pay and project margin. &nbsp;

• Shape the tooling. &nbsp;Work with engineering on task interfaces, review workflows and RL environment needs, and push for automation wherever QA is manual. &nbsp;

• Write the playbook. &nbsp;Document onboarding scripts, quality frameworks, escalation paths and pricing inputs so the next SPL ramps in weeks, not months. &nbsp;

What Y ou Have: &nbsp;

• Bachelor's Degree from an accredited college/university required &nbsp;

• An internal locus of control, high agency and grit. &nbsp;

• 1 to 5 years in consulting, banking, PE, startup operations, or delivery at a human data or AI company. &nbsp;

• A record of running projects with many moving parts and a demanding client, and shipping on time. &nbsp;

• Comfort with data. You can pull and audit a dataset in SQL, Python or a serious spreadsheet and spot what's wrong with it. &nbsp;

• Working fluency in how models are trained and evaluated: SFT, RLHF, rubrics, evals. &nbsp;

• Clear and professional writing. Specs, guidelines and status updates people act on. &nbsp;

